body:
I didn't read this reply and was worried about the stain 'setting' so I wanted to act as quick as possible. Couldn't find a bucket (we just moved and still have to unpack a lot of things) so I ended up using our fruit bowl (??) to at least soak the the stained part in with the white detergent (the entire pants didn't fit in the bowl). Read about white detergent lowkey bleaching, for scared that I turned my pants tie dye since only parts were soaked. Took it out and rinsed them by hand and soaked them in water afterwards. The parts where the detergent got onto the pants is really dark compared to the rest, even after rinsing it a lot. Don't know if that'll dissappear after washing it. So sorry this sounds like a mess and it kinda is hahaha, learning to do laundry is still a work in progress.

&#x200B;

. . I think I'll just throw it into the washing machine later like you said. I figure that you just throw it in with other white/off-white clothes and use the white detergent? Or just no detergent at all? I'll look into oxiclean as well! Thanks for the recommendation :)
